.TH "Docv::Source" "3cr" "2026-11-03" "docv 0.1.0" "docv API Reference"
.SH "NAME"
Docv::Source \- Reads page files (plain or gzip) and resolves \fB\%.so\fR and \fB\%.nx\fR includes against the page\(aqs manual tree.
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.nf
\fBrequire "docv"\fR
.sp
\fBclass Docv::Source\fR
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
Reads page files (plain or gzip) and resolves \fB\%.so\fR and \fB\%.nx\fR includes
against the page\(aqs manual tree.
.SH "CONSTRUCTORS"
.PP
\fBdef self.new(path : String | Nil = nil)\fR
.SH "CLASS METHODS"
.TP 4
\fBdef self.decode(bytes : Bytes) : String\fR
Decodes \fIbytes\fR as UTF\-8, falling back to Latin\-1.
.TP 4
\fBdef self.read(path : String) : String\fR
Reads \fIpath\fR as text, inflating gzip data and decoding invalid UTF\-8 as
Latin\-1.
.SH "INSTANCE METHODS"
.TP 4
\fBdef include(name : String) : String | Nil\fR
Reads an include; \fB\%nil\fR when it cannot be found or read.
.TP 4
\fBdef path : String | Nil\fR
The file the document came from, if any.
.TP 4
\fBdef resolve(name : String) : String | Nil\fR
Resolves an include name: relative to the manual tree root (the
directory holding \fB\%manN/\fR), then to the including file\(aqs directory.
.SH "DEFINED IN"
src/docv/source.cr
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR "Docv" (3cr),
.BR "docv" (7cr)
